<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34724" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">percontātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">percunct-</span></b> ),
		ōnis, f.
		percontor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an asking</i>, <i>inquiring</i> after
			any thing; <i>a question</i>, <i>inquiry.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen. (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tempus percontatione consumere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Univ. 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid percontationibus reperire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 5, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">percontatio quid in senatu esset actum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 60, 218</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">collocutio atque percontatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 30, 36, § 110</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., as a figure of speech, <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 3, 53, 203</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
